# TikTakToe Deployment Plan
# Adapted from RELEASE_TRAIN_EPIC.md
# Date: 2026-04-16

See DEPLOYMENT_RUNBOOK.md for required GitHub manual setup steps.

================================================================================
WILL BE USED
================================================================================

BRANCHING & RELEASE CADENCE
  - Branch naming convention: release/YYYY.WNN.D (e.g. release/2026.W17.3)
  - Weekly release train cadence:
      Mon/Tue/Wed 06:00 UTC  ->  cut candidate branch if dev is healthy
      Thu 10:00 UTC          ->  select RC, deploy to preprod (with approval)
      Thu +1 week            ->  promote preprod to prod (with approval)
  - Unused candidate branches kept forever for traceability

GITHUB ACTIONS WORKFLOWS
  - ci.yml              PR -> main: lint, type check, build, npm audit
  - deploy-dev.yml      Push -> main: build & deploy to SWA dev environment
  - cut-candidate.yml   Cron Mon/Tue/Wed: create release branch if dev healthy
  - select-rc.yml       Cron Thu: pick latest candidate, deploy to preprod
  - promote-prod.yml    Cron/manual: promote preprod to prod
  - hotfix.yml          Manual: cherry-pick fix, deploy to preprod or prod

CI STEPS (ci.yml)
  - ESLint (eslint .)
  - TypeScript type check (tsc --noEmit)
  - Production build validation (npm run build)
  - Security scan (npm audit)

GITHUB ENVIRONMENTS
  - dev       (no approval required, auto-deploy on merge to main)
  - preprod   (required reviewers: repo owners)
  - prod      (required reviewers + wait timer after preprod)

BRANCH PROTECTION (main)
  - Require pull request before merging
  - Require CI status checks to pass (ci.yml)
  - Require 1 reviewer approval
  - No force push, no direct deletions

BRANCH PROTECTION (release/**)
  - No force push (except via hotfix pipeline)
  - No deletions

OIDC WORKLOAD IDENTITY FEDERATION
  - Replace stored AZURE_STATIC_WEB_APPS_API_TOKEN secret with short-lived
    OIDC tokens scoped per environment (dev/preprod/prod)
  - No long-lived secrets stored in GitHub

ROLLBACK STRATEGY
  - Azure SWA retains prior deployments
  - Rollback = redeploy previous build via SWA CLI or portal

HOTFIX FLOW
  - Fix committed to main first (validates in dev)
  - Cherry-picked to target release branch
  - Pipeline builds and deploys to preprod or prod with approval gate

================================================================================
WILL NOT BE USED
================================================================================

INFRASTRUCTURE AS CODE (BICEP)
  - Not needed. Azure SWA is provisioned as a single managed resource.
  - No VNets, no subnets, no private endpoints to configure.
  - Modules dropped: container-registry, key-vault, storage-account,
    monitoring, container-environment, container-app, rbac, resource-group

DOCKER / CONTAINER REGISTRY (ACR)
  - Not applicable. SWA deploys static build output (dist/) directly.
  - No Dockerfile, no image tagging, no ACR push step.

AZURE CONTAINER APPS
  - Not applicable. No backend services, no containerized workloads.

MULTI-SERVICE ARCHITECTURE
  - TikTakToe is a pure SPA. No webapp, doc-index-mcp, permit-mcp services.

PROVISION PARTITION WORKFLOW (provision-partition.yml)
  - SWA environments (dev/preprod/prod) handle partition isolation natively.
  - No need to create separate resource groups or managed identities per env.

PYTHON-SPECIFIC CI STEPS
  - ruff lint/format check    (Python only)
  - pyright type check        (Python only)
  - pip-audit security scan   (Python only)
  - Tier 2 integration tests  (requires running MCP servers)

TELEMETRY GATE (App Insights availability > 99.9%)
  - Optional/deferred. App Insights not currently configured for TikTakToe.
  - Can be added later if observability requirements grow.

SEPARATE BE / FE REPOS
  - Single repo. One pipeline set covers everything.

CADDY REVERSE PROXY / LOCAL DEV SETUP
  - Not needed. Vite dev server (npm run dev) handles local development.
  - No microservices to proxy.

POWERSHELL PROVISIONING SCRIPTS
  - No legacy PowerShell scripts exist in this repo. Nothing to retire.

AZURE AD APP REGISTRATIONS / ENTRA EXTERNAL ID
  - No user authentication in TikTakToe. Not applicable.

DEPENDABOT (pip)
  - Python dependency scanning not applicable.
  - npm Dependabot can be enabled (optional, low priority).

